    "ctest": [
      "coupling.case_uniform_flow",
      "aero.uniform_flow",
      "aero.pchip_curve",
      "io.si_case"
    ],
    "catch": "Typed SI prescribed wake owns its velocity independently of ambient flow; 1 case with 680 assertions in MSVC and GCC Release, seed 23.",
    "oracle": "Signed exact ft/min rational conversion, analytical position in polynomial time, independent low-degree Hermite formula and derivatives at an interior point and a knot, zero spatial Jacobian, and rational reconstruction of projected words and radius.",
    "negative": "Free and absent wake, changed current samples at the same stamp including in-memory restoration, insufficient time coverage and work, cancellation, and failed finite projection preserving the source. Changed ambient input leaves the prescribed curve unchanged.",
    "mutation": "Byte-identical GCC 14.2 Release control at 2e871c16b4845d5d73dc100ee877636a0c4886d5: 707 assertions. Selecting ambient velocity in the prescribed branch fails 82 assertions, Catch2 exit 42. Final test-only revision removes repeated setup and boundary checks.",
    "static": "clang-format 21.1.2 and clang-tidy 21.1.1 on the two product and one test translation unit in MSVC and GCC databases."
